<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bedia Cathedral</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">999</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bedia Cathedral is a medieval church in eastern Abkhazia, founded in 999 by Bagrat III, king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abkhaz-people">Abkhazians</a> and the first king of a united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, who was buried there in 1014. Its gold Bedia Chalice, a gift of the king, is one of the masterpieces of Georgian metalwork. The church was a seat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of western Georgia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bedia-cathedral.jpg" alt="Bedia Cathedral" width="320" height="175" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Inalo1989 (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bedia2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
